            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThis was already discussed in #2028. It also contains several solutions of how to approach this.\r\n\r\nThe \"it would be a little weird to generate `g` clues for another letter, say like, `t`, but it would be nice nonetheless\" together with not wanting to single out `gen_clues.windows` are what stopping me from making this built-in.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for the suggestion!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This was already discussed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"8953188\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/2028\" data-hovercard-type=\"discussion\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/2028/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/2028\">#2028</a>. It also contains several solutions of how to approach this.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The \"it would be a little weird to generate <code class=\"notranslate\">g</code> clues for another letter, say like, <code class=\"notranslate\">t</code>, but it would be nice nonetheless\" together with not wanting to single out <code class=\"notranslate\">gen_clues.windows</code> are what stopping me from making this built-in.</p>",
